l some of the basic properties of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$:\n\n- The domain of the function is $x\\in [-1,1].$\n\n- The range of the function is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\n- Its minimum value occurs at $x=-1.$\n\n- Its maximum value occurs at $x=1.$\n\n- Its zero occurs at $x=0.$\n\n- The function is strictly increasing on its entire domain.\n\nOf the given functions, the only one that has all of these properties is as follows:\n\n![](images/df/df22eea4331c47da3047381ca672fd80ebf75118054316fe88c0e2d96dae0d34.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253293 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110569 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3e88f43c-18c5-5fdb-b6d1-579370489099" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Values in the Domain of the Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "132a7d43-69b5-5d78-bd3f-e3ed18f336c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250718} {:answer/id #uuid "7953a171-a759-565d-85cf-6fd82a5fdec8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251560} {:answer/id #uuid "90341be6-95a2-57a1-9256-6fd69e09cf38" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251777} {:answer/id #uuid "ac77906b-d8e7-58ad-9746-bb71682a0f06" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\pi " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252055} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf5091f-632c-54c6-a3c8-b3a2b127da33" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252234}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "132a7d43-69b5-5d78-bd3f-e3ed18f336c4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250718